# DTF tier manifest: api-contracts-1120-fixes
#   (artifact-keeper 1.12.0 REST API contract fixes: #4800, #4825, #4843,
#    #4834, #4851, #5201, #5652, #5694, #5487, #5347, #5223)
# Profile-set: filesystem + audit.upstream-fetches-all (AUDIT_UPSTREAM_FETCHES
# =all, so a cold HEAD's upstream contact is countable in the audit log).
# Sibling of api-contracts-1120 (features); this one holds the bug fixes.
#
# RED images (main builds; the 1.11 line either never had some of these bugs
# or took the fixes, so it cannot be the red image for all of them):
#   sha-507857f  main before #4840 (2026-10-20): every FIX except #5694
#                (whose async delete is not there yet).
#   sha-c09e5d7  main after #5316/#5331 and before #5414/#5443/#5488/#5754/
#                #5751 (2026-11-05): #5652, #5487, #5694, #5347, #5223.
# GREEN: main carrying every fix (sha-2bdf092 or later).
#
# CONTROLS (pass on every image)
#   three migration jobs, one cancelled, list with a matching total; a basic-
#   auth Remote stores and reports its credentials; a repository-owner role
#   member reads its repository while a plain user cannot change or delete
#   it; a valid visibility PATCH applies; posting the settings GET body back
#   with a new retention_days stores it; cron '30 3 * * MON' is accepted and
#   weekday '8' refused; a live repository's artifact resolves by id; a CRAN
#   Remote over a generic upstream serves a cold GET; a Remote with a
#   60-minute age hold answers a cold download 409.
#
# FIX CASES
#   #4800 GET /migrations?status= : pagination.total and total_pages count
#     only the filtered jobs.
#   #4825 a Remote create with upstream_username/password and no
#     upstream_auth_type is 400 and leaves no repository (was 201 with the
#     credentials silently dropped).
#   #4843 basic without a password, or an unknown upstream_auth_type, is 400
#     and leaves no repository, so the corrected retry is 201 (was 409).
#   #4851 the repository list (and the PATCH response) report
#     upstream_auth_type basic / upstream_auth_configured true, like the
#     detail (was null/false).
#   #4834 a repository-owner role member (role_assignments row, no
#     fine-grained rule) can PATCH, set cache-ttl on and DELETE its own
#     repositories (was 403).
#   #5201 PATCH {visibility: internal, apt_label: X} on a generic repository
#     is 400 and leaves visibility private (was 400 after saving internal).
#   #5652 GET /admin/settings reports max_upload_size_bytes 10 GiB, the limit
#     in force (was a stored 100 MB); retention_days -5 is 400 and not stored;
#     the accepted change writes one SETTING_CHANGED audit row.
#   #5487 cron '30 3 * * 0' and '0 3 * * 0-6' are accepted (0 = Sunday; was
#     400 "Invalid cron expression").
#   #5694 right after DELETE answers 202, the repository's artifacts answer
#     404 on /artifacts/{id} and /stats (was 200 until the job reached them).
#     150 artifacts keep the job running while the oracle looks.
#   #5347 a cold HEAD through a CRAN Remote records exactly one
#     UPSTREAM_FETCHED row with method HEAD (was none).
#   #5223 a release POSTed straight after a held path's 409 answers 200 and
#     the path then serves the upstream bytes (was 404 "No cached artifact at
#     that path" while the 50 MB fill was still running).
#
# The Remotes proxy the backend itself on its container address, so the SSRF
# guard needs UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS. RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~250
# quick API calls.
COVERS="4800 4825 4843 4834 4851 5201 5652 5694 5487 5347 5223"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem audit.upstream-fetches-all"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
